// Repo layer on top of the shared org preset (renovate-config:default.json5),
// covering what only this repo needs:
//
//   - github.com/dexidp/dex declares `module github.com/dexidp/dex` (no /v2), so
//     the Go toolchain ignores its real v2.x release tags and the only "releases"
//     the go datasource sees are the 2016 CoreOS-era v0.x tags. A master
//     pseudo-version (v0.0.0-…) sorts below v0.6.1, so Renovate proposes that
//     ancient tag as an "update" — a tree with no go.mod, no api/v2 and no modern
//     cmd/dex, which breaks `go mod tidy` and the e2e build. Exclude those tags.
//
//   - The e2e module runs dex from the same master commit that the root module's
//     dex/api/v2 pseudo-version points at (DESIGN.md: the last api tag predates
//     fields we use). Group the two so they move together.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  packageRules: [
    {
      matchManagers: ["gomod"],
      matchPackageNames: ["github.com/dexidp/dex"],
      allowedVersions: "!/^v?0\\./",
    },
    {
      matchManagers: ["gomod"],
      matchPackageNames: ["github.com/dexidp/dex", "github.com/dexidp/dex/api/v2"],
      groupName: "dex",
    },
  ],
}
